content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-103 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22410, filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end housing vibration is exactly 7.1 mm/s RMS. The applicable HF-300 bearing-housing vibration boundary is 7.1 mm/s RMS: Zone C is 4.5–7.1 and requires restricted operation with maintenance planned, while Zone D is 7.1–11.0 and says damage is likely and to stop the pump. The figure expressly does not establish which zone owns an exact boundary value. This work order therefore applies the Zone D stop response conservatively, without claiming a definitive zone classification.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The reported 72°C housing temperature is 2°C above the bearing-housing normal limit of up to 70°C, but remains 8°C below the 80°C alarm and 18°C below the 90°C trip. Thus it is above normal but does not reach either documented temperature alarm or trip limit. The manual specifies that bearing temperatures are measured on the housing surface.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Only the drive-end vibration reading is reported. The condition-monitoring procedure requires vibration velocity on both bearing housings and classification of the highest reading, so the supplied reading alone is not a complete both-housing classification.",
      "citations": [
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leak is reported, so the troubleshooting symptom 'leakage at shaft seal' is not present. That row does not, by itself, justify routine seal replacement for this fault; it also does not prove that the seal is free from other damage.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Investigate bearing wear first as a leading, unconfirmed candidate: it is documented as a cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature, matching the combination of boundary-level vibration and above-normal housing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Misalignment is the other leading candidate because it is also listed for both high vibration and high bearing temperature. No alignment measurements are supplied, so it cannot yet be distinguished from bearing wear.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing is a documented cause of high bearing temperature; check grease quantity. It is not listed in the supplied troubleshooting row as a cause of high vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage remains a documented high-vibration cause and requires impeller inspection.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation remains a documented high-vibration cause; check NPSH. No suction-condition or NPSH results are supplied to elevate or exclude this cause.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop P-103 now and hold it out of service pending inspection and technical disposition. This is the conservative work-order response to the unresolved 7.1 mm/s RMS Zone C/D boundary, using Zone D's 'damage likely—stop the pump' action; it is not a definitive boundary classification.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Review available condition-monitoring records for both bearing housings and identify the highest reading. Record that this report contains only the 7.1 mm/s RMS drive-end value; the manual's routine method uses both housings and classifies the highest reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before authorising return to service, check shaft alignment, inspect the bearings and impeller, check NPSH for possible cavitation, and check grease quantity. Record inspection results rather than treating any listed probable cause as already diagnosed.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair: drive-end HF3-512, bearing 6312-C3, and non-drive-end HF3-510, bearing 6310-C3. Do not replace only the drive-end bearing when this trigger is met.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If seal replacement is added after inspection, isolate and drain the pump, remove the back pull-out assembly, remove the impeller nut and impeller, and withdraw the seal and sleeve. For serial HF3-22410, do not fit HF3-450; fit pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B, with no sleeve measurement needed for seal setting. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth, fit a new casing gasket, and tighten the HF3-450B seal gland nut to 30 Nm. Obtain the manual's Table 5 values for other fasteners before reassembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Whenever the casing is opened, including work other than seal replacement, install a new HF3-120 casing gasket.",
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment. Acceptance tolerances are 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular offset.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; one required as part of the conditional bearing-pair replacement set if either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; one required with HF3-512 because the bearings must be replaced as a pair when the documented trigger is met.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; replace whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Conditional part only if seal replacement is added: pre-set cartridge mechanical seal, mandatory replacement for HF3-450 on this serial-range pump; gland nut torque 30 Nm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Conditional shaft sleeve for seal work; replace if sleeve scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "P-103 falls within P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line, which is chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite. Establish the site chemical controls before opening or draining the pump; the supplied evidence does not specify those controls.",
      "citations": [
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For mechanical-seal replacement, isolate and drain the pump before removing the back pull-out assembly and seal components.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly has a documented mass of 68 kg and lifting equipment is required. The pump's back pull-out design allows the rotating assembly to be removed without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The seal flush arrangement is Plan 11 from pump discharge; never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing-pair replacement: 6.0 hours with 2 technicians. Inspection must first establish the repair scope; this is not an unconditional allowance for replacing only one bearing.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional laser alignment after work moving the motor or bearing housing: 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional mechanical-seal replacement, only if that scope is added: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal manual versus bulletin: the generic manual parts list identifies component seal HF3-450 and the manual procedure refers reassembly fasteners to Table 5. SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, expressly applies to HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. Serial HF3-22410 is within that range, so the bulletin governs this asset: do not fit HF3-450; use HF3-450B and its 30 Nm gland-nut torque instead of the superseded 25 Nm value. The below-HF3-22000 exception does not apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration-zone ambiguity: Figure 3 places 7.1 mm/s RMS at both the upper end of Zone C and the lower end of Zone D and explicitly provides no boundary-ownership rule. No other supplied chunk resolves that ambiguity. The execution decision for this order is the conservative Zone D stop response, while the definitive zone classification remains an open question.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Which zone officially owns a reading of exactly 7.1 mm/s RMS? The supplied figure does not say, so manufacturer or documented site clarification is needed for a definitive classification; the immediate stop is an interim conservative decision (C06, C07).",
    "What is the non-drive-end bearing-housing vibration reading, and do existing records contain any higher reading on either housing? Both housings are required for the routine survey and the highest reading must be classified (C06).",
    "Which housing produced the 72°C temperature reading, and was it measured on the housing surface as specified by the manual? The report does not explicitly identify the temperature location (C01).",
    "What are the alignment readings, bearing wear/noise findings, grease quantity, impeller condition and NPSH/cavitation findings? The evidence lists checks and possible causes but does not establish the actual root cause (C09).",
    "What NPSH acceptance criterion and what grease specification/correct grease quantity should the technician use? The supplied troubleshooting table requires these checks but provides neither criterion nor grease specification (C09).",
    "Does the above-normal but below-alarm 72°C reading, by itself, constitute the 'high temperature' trigger for mandatory bearing-pair replacement, or is replacement to be based on confirmed inspection findings? The supplied chunks do not define that term beyond the normal/alarm/trip table (C02, C10).",
    "If casing or seal reassembly is required, what are all other applicable Table 5 fastener torques? Table 5 is not supplied; only the HF3-450B gland-nut torque of 30 Nm is documented, and it must not be assumed to apply to other fasteners (C10, C13).",
    "What site-specific isolation, PPE, draining, flushing and disposal controls are required for the sodium hypochlorite-dosed line? The evidence establishes the chemical dosing but not those procedures (C16).",
    "How much time should be allowed for diagnosis/inspection and what is the total downtime? Table 6 gives standard labour only for seal replacement, bearing-pair replacement and laser alignment, not for troubleshooting or inspection, and the final repair scope remains conditional (C12)."
  ]
}
